TITLE:: PltCut
summary:: The events an onset threshold makes, at every threshold
categories:: Libraries>PlotLib
related:: Overviews/PlotLib, Classes/PltNovelty, Classes/PltConditioning

DESCRIPTION::
A detection function and the events it yields, one row per threshold from code::lo::
to code::hi::. An event that persists down many rows is strongly in the signal; one
that appears, vanishes and comes back belongs as much to the threshold and the
minimum gap as to the sound. The bars in the right margin count the events at each
threshold.

Above, the curve at the chosen cut: ink above the threshold, muted below it, where
the detector discards what it measured. The caption gives the share of the curve that
falls below. Click or drag in the raster to move the cut.

The picking is link::Classes/PltNovelty::'s: a local maximum above the threshold,
with anything within code::minGap:: of the last pick suppressed.

